PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Family Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Pass a decree of Restitution of Conjugal Rights under Section 9 of the Hindu Marriage Act, 1955 in favour of the Petitioner and against the Respondent, directing the Respondent to resume cohabitation and return to the matrimonial home with the Petitioner;
(b) Award costs of the petition to the Petitioner;
(c) Grant such other or further relief as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the facts and grounds stated hereinabove, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Admit the present Criminal Appeal and call for the lower court records of Sessions Case No. [NUMBER] from the Court of learned Sessions Judge, [PLACE];
(b) Set aside and quash the impugned judgment of conviction and order of sentence dated [DATE] passed by the learned Sessions Judge in Sessions Case No. [NUMBER];
(c) Acquit the Appellant of all charges under Sections [SECTIONS];
(d) Suspend the sentence of the Appellant and enlarge the Appellant on bail under Section 389 CrPC during the pendency of the appeal;
(e) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Conduct a preliminary enquiry under Section 340 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 into the deliberate falsehood and forged documents filed by the Respondent in the present proceedings;
(b) Record a finding that the Respondent has committed offences punishable under Sections 191, 192, 193, 209, and 471 of the Indian Penal Code affecting the administration of justice;
(c) Direct an Officer of this Hon'ble Court to file a formal written criminal complaint before the competent Judicial Magistrate having jurisdiction for prosecution of the Respondent;
(d) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, in light of the supervening circumstances stated hereinabove, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Exercise jurisdiction under Section 439(2) of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 and cancel the bail granted to Respondent No. 2/Accused vide order dated [DATE] in FIR No. [NUMBER]/[YEAR];
(b) Direct that Respondent No. 2 be taken into judicial custody forthwith for blatant violation of bail conditions and threatening prosecution witnesses;
(c) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

PRAYER:
WHEREFORE, it is most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble High Court may graciously be pleased to:
(a) Grant Special Leave to Appeal under Section 378(4) of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 to the Appellant/Complainant against the impugned judgment of acquittal dated [DATE] passed by the learned [MAGISTRATE COURT] in CC No. [NUMBER];
(b) Set aside and reverse the impugned judgment of acquittal and convict Respondent No. 1 for the offence punishable under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881;
(c) Direct Respondent No. 1 to pay the cheque amount along with statutory interest and compensation to the Appellant;
(d) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit.
